    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d116-a1">

                <pb facs="0288" n="192" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg192"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure No. 3 in No. 66.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. de España to Mr. Luedor.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-08-22"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 22,
                        1878</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 297.]</seg></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">C. Luedor</hi>, Esq.,<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">Consul-General for Germany, and Doyen of the Consular
                        Corps, Shanghai:</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to forward you a note to
                    the chamber of commerce at Shanghai, in response to the statement of Messrs.
                    Butterfield &amp; Swire, relative to the measures taken by the Chinese
                    authorities with respect to their hulk at the port of Chinkiang, which, at the
                    request of the consular corps, you did me the favor of transmitting with your
                    letter of 8th of this month.</p>
                <p>Receive, Mr. Consul-General and Doyen, the assurances of my distinguished
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">de</hi> ESPAÑA.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
